        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Replacing a sump pump in an existing pit typically costs a few hundred to about a thousand dollars, while a new pit through the slab runs roughly $1,500 to $4,000 before any drain tile. A battery backup adds several hundred to over a thousand more. Prices vary by region and change, so get itemized quotes and compare scope, not just totals.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Spend where it matters: a well-sized cast iron pump, a new check valve, a discharge line that carries water well away from the house, and an alarm or backup if your basement is finished. Replace the pump on a schedule rather than in the middle of a storm, and you will pay the low end of these ranges instead of the high end.
          </p>
